From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:01:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] client: expose ordered observations and joined shutdown

Install a synchronous observer before workers start, report each received
query-set transition and connection state, and report terminal closure
without turning snapshots into a database change log. Keep the existing
bounded state channel best effort so a full receiver cannot block
reconnects or shutdown.

Give cloned clients one cancellation-safe joined close operation covering
both background tasks, retain final-drop cancellation, and preserve
buffered stream and submitted-mutation semantics. A closed protocol
response channel terminates the query worker and pending requests even
with live client clones. Join the transport and retain its panic for close
to report. End the transport when its request stream closes, including
while it waits for reconnect acknowledgement.

Preserve mutation visibility ordering: complete successful mutations only
after a query transition reaches their commit timestamp. Complete plain
and structured errors immediately and remove them from reconnect replay.
Ignore legitimate late repeated mutation responses after completion while
retaining future-ID and active request-type validation. These completion
and duplicate-response corrections are independently authored.

Adapt terminal worker progress handling from upstream PR #16:
https://github.com/get-convex/convex-rs/pull/16
Source commit: 8c0e01c56b4f7f507595ec2eddee22f19fc5e7d4
Use transport closure as terminal within the existing shared shutdown
owner rather than introducing a separate retry or task-lifecycle API.

Add local WebSocket lifecycle, completion-order, late-response and terminal
OCC fixtures. Document the replay, observation and immutable source
revision distribution boundaries. The fixtures model successful-result
retention; they do not establish real-backend deduplication retention.

Co-authored-by: David Potgieter <2729962+david-potgieter@users.noreply.github.com>
